WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.719
If you want to hear the details about Patrick's
life that had to be taken out of the movies

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.840
because they were way, way too dark for audiences,
then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.060
[Intro]

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.210
I wasn't planning on doing another It character
on Horror History, at least not for a while,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.620
but I got so many requests to cover Patrick
Hockstetter, the twisted preteen with no sense

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.820
of morality making him the scariest human
character in the novel.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.020
One thing that Stephen King makes note of
is the fact that Patrick’s behaviour probably

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.460
would have been picked up on by child psychologists
had he been born in a later era, so in today’s

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.720
episode, we’ll attempt to analyse Patrick
with a psychological lens.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.640
To fully understand him, we’ve first gotta first
take it back to his childhood.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.000
[HORROR HISTORY]

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.740
Patrick Hockstetter was born in 1946 as the son of paint salesman, Patrick’s father,

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.090
and Patrick’s mother who is only described
as being a devout Catholic.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.110
Patrick is a plump boy with a perfectly round,
pallid moonface, much different than the slender

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.660
looking Hot Topic version of Patrick from
the theatrical version.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.230
Patrick developed a psychiatric condition
called Solipsism Syndrome, which is when a

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.260
person feels that there is no reality beyond
their own mind.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.619
Patrick believed that he was real, but that
he was the only real person.

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:11.290
Nobody but him actually existed, they were
just figments of his own mind.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:14.880
The novel never explains how Patrick developed
this disorder, but I would guess it may have

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.590
been related to the birth of his younger brother,
Avery, in late 1950, because Solipsism Syndrome

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:24.060
has been associated with periods of extended
isolation, most often diagnosed in astronauts

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.299
left alone for long missions in outer space.

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:30.090
Perhaps when Avery was born, he commanded
all of Mr. and Mrs. Hockstetter’s attention

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.539
and left Patrick feeling isolated, maybe even
neglected, and due to his young age -- he

00:01:34.539 --> 00:01:38.249
was only five at the time -- the effects of
Solipsism set in more quickly.

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:40.840
Patrick did not like when Avery was brought
home from the hospital.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.359
He claimed not to care if his parents had
more kids, as long as his schedule was not

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:48.369
interrupted, and he began to feel jealous
as his meals started coming in late and Avery’s

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:51.810
crying kept him awake at night as his parents
constantly tended to the newborn.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.450
It is not known to what extent his parents
neglect reached, but Patrick did begin to

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.100
fear that Avery would replace him, so he took
matters into his own hands one day when he

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.630
came home from Kindergarten.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.369
His father was at work, and his mother was
napping, so he wandered into Avery’s room.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:07.979
What the five year old Patrick did next is
considered to be one of the most disturbing

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:10.600
chapters in all of Stephen King’s writing.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.129
He started by turning Avery’s head into
the pillow.

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:17.040
He stood there and watched him struggle for
air for 5 minutes before Avery managed to

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.069
turn his head back up.

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:21.569
Then he tried holding Avery’s face down
into the pillow, testing if the baby’s snorts

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:23.250
for air would wake up Mrs. Hockstetter.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.299
They didn’t.

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:28.219
So he decided to press Avery’s face down
into the pillow full force, and did not let

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:29.219
go.

00:02:29.219 --> 00:02:33.099
The feeling of doing this excited Patrick
in a way he had never felt before.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:37.079
After the deed was done, he casually strolled
downstairs and made himself a plate of cookies

00:02:37.079 --> 00:02:38.079
with a glass of milk.

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:41.700
When his mother woke up, she came downstairs
before checking on Avery, thinking he was

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.700
still asleep.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.799
Patrick showed her the drawing he had made
at school, which was just a chaotic mess of

00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:46.849
black and brown scribbles.

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:48.480
He told her it was a house and tree.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.909
He would bring home the same mess scrawling
lines every day, each time telling her it’s

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:53.909
something else.

00:02:53.909 --> 00:02:57.099
These drawings are never explained, but they
may be an indicator of Patrick’s stalled

00:02:57.099 --> 00:02:59.519
development in response to his solipsism.

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:03.540
Age children age, they not only physically
develop and grow from babies, to kids, to

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.640
teens, to adults, but there is also an emotional
development taking place.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.999
However, if a child had solipsism like Patrick,
he never makes those emotional connections

00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:14.019
with other humans, because he believes he
is the only human.

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:15.629
So he becomes of sociopath.

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:19.069
Children’s drawings are one way that they’re
able to express their emotions.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:23.129
From a young age, such as 2 or 3, they may
express themselves more through the process

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:24.540
than the final product.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.749
So if they are trying to draw a car, they
might scribble a bunch of fast lines across

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:28.749
the page.

00:03:28.749 --> 00:03:32.400
But by age 5, they are able to understand
how to create shapes and somewhat realistic

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.420
proportions, because their motor skills have
developed, and they’ve emotionally developed

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.750
to want to make something more complex.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.400
But in Patrick’s case, he hasn’t emotionally
evolved at all, probably not since his parents

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.630
started thinking about having a second child.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:48.330
Mrs. Hockstetter was worried by his disturbing
artwork, but she just told herself he would

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.480
grow out of it and tried to ignore the problem.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.579
She didn’t discover Avery’s death until
5PM, when she went to check on his unusually

00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:55.879
lengthy nap.

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:59.299
Patrick sat watching TV through the uproar
of screaming and crying that followed.

00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:03.099
The doctor came at some point to see if there
was any chance to save Avery, and when he

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:06.810
saw Patrick’s nonchalant reaction, he assumed
that he’d gone into some kind of state of

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.489
shock and gave him a pill for it.

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:10.290
The incident was diagnosed as a crib-death.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.709
There was a moment where Mr. Hockstetter noticed
what looked to be Patrick’s snowy footprints

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:18.459
in Avery’s room, and almost put two and
two together, but then forced himself to push

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:19.459
that thought away.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:23.550
But perhaps what has really chilled readers
is that over the remaining 7 years of Patrick’s

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:28.750
life, he felt no shame, no guilt and experienced
no nightmares over what he had done.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.430
In 1951, he began his first attempt at first
grade.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:34.870
He was seeking to recapture the feeling that
he enjoyed so much that he discovered at the

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.539
side of Avery’s crib, so he started a little
collection in his pencil box.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:41.800
He would kill flies and torture beatles, and
keep them in this box.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.590
It was a microcosm for another distressing
habit of his later in life, involving a refrigerator

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.590
at the dump.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.870
On the way home one day, he discovered a dying
cat that had been run over, and an old woman

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.840
caught him poking at it and told him off.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.990
If only he had lived a little way down the
road over in Ludlow, Maine, he would have

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:57.260
loved it over there.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.140
*growl*

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.480
"Ahh!"

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.860
Patrick was forced to repeat the first grade
during the 1951-1952 school year, but the

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:08.099
following summer, on a family trip, he would
discover the only semblance of a true fear

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.480
that he would ever encounter.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.300
In August of 1953, the Hockstetter family
visited Brewster Lake.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.910
One day when Patrick was swimming out in the lake,
he got out to discover leeches stuck to his

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:23.440
body.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.480
Not those leeches.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.900
The other ones.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:29.120
Leeches are the blood sucking worm parasite
found in some freshwater lakes.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.790
Patrick did not like the idea of having his
blood sucked because it reminded him of his

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:36.620
mortality, and he believed he could not die
because he was the only real person.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.810
So he screamed and screamed until his dad
pulled off the leeches.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.419
This was the one and only thing that ever
scared him, and it is described in the book

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:44.819
as a wretched loathing.

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:48.169
Patrick managed to get through second grade
on one try, but the same could not be said

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:50.129
about third grade with Mrs. Weems.

00:05:50.129 --> 00:05:53.569
As he got older, his strange behaviour became
more and more apparent.

00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:57.310
Mrs. Weems knew about the pencil box filled
with flies whose wings had been removed by

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:01.199
Patrick, but he was quiet and didn’t really
have any disruptive disciplinary issues, so

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:05.151
it was easy for him to fly under the radar
compared to kids like Henry Bowers who would

00:06:05.151 --> 00:06:06.340
disrupt class and start fights.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.970
That’s not to say that Patrick had no issues.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.870
Sometimes he would turn in his tests completely
blank, or just with a large question mark,

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.400
like Nathan Explosion during his GED.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.080
"Let's see here. OK.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.920
“It’s a zero.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.780
No questions were answered.”

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.520
“Ah.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:24.960
Damn!

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.220
Seriously?”

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.910
“How could you have not known that?”

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.200
So he had to repeat the third grade as well.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.240
I guess he had some Bruce Bochy even year
magic in him, because he managed to pass the fourth

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.940
grade, and then it was in the fifth grade,
in October of 1957 that he made one major

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:41.540
upgrade to his pencil box hobby by finding
an abandoned refrigerator in the dump and

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.670
made it his new experimentation lab.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.949
He would kidnap the pets of his neighbors
in a cardboard carton and bring them to the

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:50.750
refrigerator to do horrible things to them,
all in the name of recapturing the feeling

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.650
he’d gotten on Avery’s final afternoon.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.340
He captured several pets and strays over the
course of the next 8 months, discarding the

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.430
bodies in the bushes after he was through
with them.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:02.409
But as his need for a fix increased, he started
to suspect that someone knew about what he

00:07:02.409 --> 00:07:03.409
was doing.

00:07:03.409 --> 00:07:04.690
The fridge grew a power over him.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:09.000
He seems to develop some kind of ritual associated
with opening it, which is only seen once by

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.139
Beverly Marsh from a distance and described
as a swaying motion “like a guy in a horror

00:07:13.139 --> 00:07:15.500
movie trying to summon a dead body out of
a crypt.”

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.250
He would fantasize about the fridge during
the day, drawing pictures of it in school

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.979
and dreaming of it during the night.

00:07:20.979 --> 00:07:24.479
In one dream, the fridge was huge and he opened
it to find a it contained a pair of eyes staring

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:25.479
at him.

00:07:25.479 --> 00:07:27.669
This may be related to his worry that somebody
knew about him.

00:07:27.669 --> 00:07:31.590
When he ran out of pets to torture, he moved
onto pidgeons and any other animals he could

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.939
find to satisfy his craving.

00:07:32.939 --> 00:07:37.020
In 5th grade, he had Mrs. Douglass, and she
had to deal with some new problems that his

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.349
previous teachers had not.

00:07:38.349 --> 00:07:42.689
She kept him away from girls on the seating
chart because of his tendency to get handsy.

00:07:42.689 --> 00:07:45.090
Beverly was one of the girls who had to experience
this.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:51.550
“...all at once you’d feel this hand . . . almost
as light as a feather, but warm and sweaty.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:52.690
Meaty.”

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:55.919
Pennywise is pretty scary dude, but I’m
starting to think he’s got nothing on Meatyhands

00:07:55.919 --> 00:07:57.620
Hockstetter over.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.240
What do you even have to do to get your hands
to feel meaty--

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.000
“And the worst thing—the horrible thing—was
the way he’d smile and never say anything.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.430
Mrs. Douglas knew.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:09.850
Greta Bowie told on him, and I think Sally
Mueller said something once, too.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:12.629
But . . . I think Mrs. Douglas was scared
of him, too.”

00:08:12.629 --> 00:08:15.680
Needless to say, Patrick did not pass the
5th grade.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.920
“NOOOO!!!!”

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.590
Perhaps it was this fear that Mrs. Douglas
had of him that was the reason he was allowed

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.230
to take summer school rather than repeating
yet another grade, but these summer classes

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:30.699
did not stop him from terrorizing the kids
of Derry during July of 1958.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:34.410
Not only had Patrick reached full fledged
psychopath status by now, but he was also

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:38.390
spending his free time with other troubled
kids and had become a member of Henry Bowers

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:39.640
feared gang of bullies.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:43.040
On July 20th, they were chasing down a boy
named Eddie Kaspbrak.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.590
Henry was desperate for revenge on Eddie for
the part he played in a rock fight earlier

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.590
that summer.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.170
When they caught up with him, Patrick, who
had no real beef with Eddie but enjoyed causing

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.860
others to feel pain, slapped his face on both
sides.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:57.410
Henry ended up breaking Eddie’s arm, and
when police sirens could be heard in the distance,

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:01.130
they decided to split, but before running
for it Patrick left Eddie with a little parting

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.940
gift by spitting in his face.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.920
This was the ultimate attack when it comes
to Eddie, who was a known hypochondriac and

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:07.920
germaphobe.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.420
I imagine Patrick took great pleasure in what
would be taken as such a hurtful act.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.550
Later that month, Patrick is hanging out with
the Bowers Gang again and suggests they go

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:15.550
to the dump.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:19.200
They all have their parts around the ankles
as they try to ignite their farts with a lighter.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.470
After some time, Henry’s minions Belch and
Victor have to leave, so just Henry and Patrick

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:24.470
remain.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:29.200
Henry takes a turn being the… ahem…. the
Fuel source and Patrick gets to close and

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:32.810
burns his… uhh… exhaust pipe?

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.140
And he gets pissed.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.370
Patrick offers to show something to Henry,
telling him it will feel good.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.470
So he ends up giving him a “hand”, and
also giving himself a “hand” at the same

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.160
time.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:45.660
They’re both enjoying themselves, so Patrick
offers to take it a step further by doing

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.320
a little… pipe… cleaning…?

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:52.530
And Henry kind of realizes what he’s gotten
himself into and lashes out to knock Patrick

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.380
to the ground and tells him that he doesn’t
go for any of that stuff.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:59.770
They argue over whether or not Henry liked
it, and Patrick had a crazy smile on until

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:03.690
Henry dropped a bombshell on him, that would
make one of Patrick’s biggest worries come

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:04.360
true.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:14.260
After the… pipe examination… incident…

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:17.980
Henry threatens Patrick to try to get him
to stay quiet about it, and Patrick basically

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.800
blackmails him, asking for $1 in exchange
for silence.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:25.340
But little does he know, Henry has a counter
of his own, saying if Hockstetter tells, he’ll

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:28.730
tell everyone about what Patrick does at the
refrigerator and get him thrown in a mental

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.730
asylum.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.230
This is the only time in the book where Patrick
sounds kind of scared while he responds -- not

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.270
the same fear as his fear of leeches, but
more of a worry about getting caught, because

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:39.440
he knows that breaking rules means consequences.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:43.330
With that, Henry leaves, forgetting to take
with his lighter as he did.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.400
Patrick continued to sit there for the next
five minutes playing with the lighter, pants

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.460
still at his ankles.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.091
You’d think someone who is afraid of leeches
might also be bit conscious about ticks, but

00:10:51.091 --> 00:10:52.091
apparently not.

00:10:52.091 --> 00:10:56.070
A few minutes later he returned to the refrigerator
to check on a pidgeon he’d caught two days

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.070
before.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:59.630
He wanted to discard the corpse because of
Henry’s threat and perhaps clean out the

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.730
inside of the fridge as well, just in case.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:05.690
When he opened the door, he saw that the pigeon
was all skeletal, the meat was completely

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:09.200
picked off of it’s bones, and the inner
walls of the fridge were covered in small

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.390
flesh colored creatures that Patrick thought
looked like Macaroni shells.

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:15.570
One of these creatures latched onto his arm
and slowly turned red.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.830
He still didn’t think it was harmful because
he still believed it was not real.

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:23.190
But then he came to a realization about what
they were: some kind of flying leeches, his

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:25.340
worst fear, but with wings.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.790
Yeah, that’s pretty scary to think about.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:31.770
He screamed, and swatted at the thing, which
was growing in size, and it bursted, but to

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:35.160
his horror, the head remained in tact and
was still clenched to his arm.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:38.630
He had to pry the thing off using his fingers,
(which is actually what you’re supposed

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.630
to do).

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.530
Then the other leeches flew out of the fridge
and attacked him.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:45.980
As usual, he felt no pain, just a draining
sensation, and stark terror.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.280
One flew down his shirt.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:49.900
Another landed on his eye and began draining
it’s fluids.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.740
One went inside his mouth and feasted on his
tongue.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.190
Some of them, including the one in his mouth
burst upon reaching capacity.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.490
He lost so much blood he began to get woozy.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:01.150
He fell to the ground and rolled over and
over.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.180
Before passing out, he saw a figure.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:07.080
This was IT, the shapeshifting entity that
takes the form of it’s victim’s greatest

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:07.940
fear.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.880
“...as the figure drew closer, he saw its
face was running like wax.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:14.060
Sometimes it began to harden and look like
something—or someone—and then it would

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:18.040
start to run again, as if it couldn’t make
up its mind who or what it wanted to be.”

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:22.350
I think that Patrick was just so psychologically
messed up that It was unable to find another

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:24.150
fear for Patrick that would be suitable.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:27.870
While there wasn’t another form that he
feared, he was afraid of an idea, which was

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:28.970
the idea of his death.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:33.110
He believed that if he died, all others would
die because he was the only real person.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:36.330
I guess the leeches were a strong enough form
to do Patrick in though.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:40.550
Just goes to show that even the craziest psychopaths
have at least one thing they are afraid of.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.180
I get chills every time.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:46.160
The shapeshifting It said only one thing to
him: “Hello and Goodbye.”

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.370
before dragging Patrick’s body to the Barrens.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.900
He passed out on the way there.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:51.900
When he awoke again, he was inside of the
sewers.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:54.410
It had already begun feeding on him.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.270
There’s not a whole lot more I can say about
the life of Patrick Hockstetter.

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:01.440
We’re only given clues about the origin
of his solipsism that put a dark cloud over

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:05.430
his youthful development and shaped him into
a homicidal sociopath and on the way to becoming

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.630
the full-blown psycho as a pre-teen.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:11.110
However his issues started, it’s clear that
they continued because of his increasing need

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.150
to feed his addiction.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:16.460
The movies do paint Patrick to be a sadistic
character with some scary issues, but don’t

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:20.400
attempt to come close to the dark and disturbing
details of Patrick’s life in the novel.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.700
Hopefully this analysis of him did him
justice.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.870
And by the way, let me know who else you’d
like to see covered here on Horror History,

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:28.100
or what franchise you’d like to see me cover.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.690
And if you haven’t already seen it, the
